<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle $1-$3 lower - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle $1-$3 lower - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers sold $1.00-$3.00 per cwt lower in Monday's market in light trading for a limited early week supply, USDA said.</p>
<p>Offerings mixed, mostly small lots native cattle of rather plain quality, although including some fleshy attractive yearling cattle. Demand fair. 97 percent over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Steers; Medium and Large 1 lot 502 lbs 87.50, lot 635 lbs 80.00, lot 714 lbs 75.25, lot 821 lbs 74.50, lot 892 lbs 70.85, fleshy 1050- 1100 lbs 65.10-67.00, fleshy 1150-1200 lbs 62.50-64.90, including 117 head shipment at latter price.</p>
<p>Heifers Medium and Large 1 lot 574 lbs 78.00, lot 714 lbs 74.00, lot 774 lbs 65.00, lot 844 lbs 65.50, 850-900 lbs 64.20-66.50, including some fleshy, lot Blk-BlkWf 69.50, part load 917 lbs 65.90.</p>
